RF.put("questb:b10",{"8170":{"id":8170,"t":"The Battle for Arathi Basin!","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Assault the Arathi Basin mine, lumber mill, blacksmith and stable, and then return to Deathmaster Dwire in Hammerfall.\nMine Assaulted\nLumber Mill Assaulted\nBlacksmith Assaulted\nStable Assaulted","desc":"As you no doubt have heard, the League of Arathor is sending large numbers of troops into Arathi Basin. Eager for food and supplies, these Alliance fools are intent to take and control the rich resources there. We must show them that Arathi will never again be a home for humans!\nGo to Arathi Basin and assault the mine, the lumber mill, the blacksmith and the stables. Pull down the enemies' banners, declaring those territories for the Horde.\nGo, ‹name›. Report back to me when this task is complete.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+200 reputation with The Defilers","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.3,"y":29.7,"n":"Deathmaster Dwire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8730":{"id":8730,"t":"Nefarius's Corruption","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Nefarian and recover the Red Scepter Shard. Return the Red Scepter Shard to Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris. You have 5 hours to complete this task.\nRed Scepter Shard Nefarian","desc":"Champion, is it you? A thousand years it has been since I was entrusted the shard and it is at my darkest hour that one should rise to relieve me of it... But what would tragedy be without cruelty?\n<Vaelastrasz coughs weakly.>\nNe... Nefarius now holds the scepter shard.\nTime is of the essence. Nefarius plans to destroy the shard. You must hurry!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOnyx Embedded Leggings Amulet of Shadow Shielding\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Another of our heroes lost to the spawn of Deathwing. We will be cursed with this suffering forever...","done":"Vaelastrasz's soul is at ease, champion. The Aspects all watch your progress with great interest. Know that you have powerful allies.\nI was commanded to grant you something to aid you in this struggle. Use it well...\nTanaris Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1}],"cats":["blackwing-lair"]},"97930":{"id":97930,"t":"Camping 101 engineering","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Twizwick Sprocketgrind in the Venture Co. Mine in Mulgore to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your engineering skill to 20","desc":"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.\nLevel 6 , requires level 4 Difficulty 4 9 12 Side Horde Quest ID 97930","cats":["camping"]},"94330":{"id":94330,"t":"Craftsmans writ darkrune gauntlets","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Darkrune Gauntlets\nDarkrune Gauntlets","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Darkrune Gauntlets, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Darkrune Gauntlets Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94330","cats":["crafting"]},"94250":{"id":94250,"t":"Craftsmans writ small silk pack","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Small Silk Pack\nSmall Silk Pack","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Small Silk Pack, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Yo! Is that pack for me?","done":"Ha ha! Thanks, pal. I owe you.\n<Kzixx reaches into a Small Silk Pack already in his possession, filled to the brim with coin, and pulls out a fist full. He counts out a tiny fraction of his total wealth, and hands it to you.>\nThis should cover it. No take-backs!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":81.7,"y":19.9,"n":"Kzixx","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"7930":{"id":7930,"t":"5 Tickets - Darkmoon Flower","lv":60,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Item #19182","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Flower","back":"Step right up, step right up! If you have tickets from the Darkmoon Faire you'd like redeemed, then just say so! You can redeem tickets in various denominations for wondrous and fantastic prizes. Don't be shy, give it a try!\nItem #19182 (5)","done":"Here you go, here you go! A prize fit for a king! Congratulations to you, my friend!\nIf you have more tickets you'd like to turn in, then please let me know! For as long as the Darkmoon Faire is here, I'll redeem your tickets.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"4730":{"id":4730,"t":"Beached Sea Creature","lv":16,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Sea Creature Bones to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\nSea Creature Bones Beached Sea Creature\nProvided: Sea Creature Bones","desc":"The half-devoured corpse of what might have been a giant sea mammal lies on the beach. A band of murlocs, stronger than those found closer to Auberdine, have taken up residence around the fallen creature. Enough of the creature remains that a suitable sample of its bones could be delivered to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.","rew":"Money: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 575\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello again, ‹name›! Are you here to report on another discovery?","done":"The bones you have are from gentle sea mammals that are known to inhabit the waters surrounding the base of Teldrassil. They had never been known to violently beach themselves like the threshers had been known to. Why would these creatures do this, I wonder? Well, perhaps the study of their remains will bear the fruits of knowledge that we seek.\nAgain, thank you for your aid. Please accept this honorarium from the Temple of the Moon.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":32.7,"y":80.8,"n":"Beached Sea Creature","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"970":{"id":970,"t":"The Tower of Althalaxx","lv":21,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect a Glowing Soul Gem and return it to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post.\nGlowing Soul Gem Dark Strand Assassin 2 % , Dark Strand Excavator 2 % , Dark Strand Adept 2 % , Dark Strand Enforcer 2 % and 1 more","desc":"Balthule's letter is dire. This Cult of the Dark Strand is a thorn in my side that must be removed. I have been dealing with some of the Dark Strand scum northeast of here at Ordil'Aran. One of their number possesses a soul gem that I believe holds the secret to the cult's power.\nBring it to me, and I will be able to decipher the secrets held within.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you acquired that soul gem?","done":"Hmm, some dark magic enchants this soulstone. Let's see what's trapped inside, shall we?","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Delgren the Purifier","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"730":{"id":730,"t":"Trouble In Darkshore?","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Auberdine and look for signs of the dwarven excavation team.","desc":"How nice it is to see a ‹class› interested in the great archeological wonders of our world.\nOftentimes our work is dismissed as mere hobby by our friends in the Alliance. But what many fail to realize is that recent discoveries in Khaz Modan have proven that a great and powerful force threatens all of Azeroth, from Lordaeron to Kalimdor.\nI am most worried about my crew that I sent to Darkshore. They haven't sent word in weeks.\nTravel to Auberdine and look for a clue as to their whereabouts.","rew":"Experience: 490\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","done":"I'm so glad Chief Archeologist Greywhisker sent for us....\nDarnassus Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":31.2,"y":84.5,"n":"Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":41.8,"n":"Archaeologist Hollee","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"1370":{"id":1370,"t":"Stealing Supplies","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 bags of Crudely Dried Meat to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village.\n6 Crudely Dried Meat Sack of Meat\nReach 3000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"When we are not at war, we hunt for meat. Meat gives us strength, and full bellies fight harder than empty ones.\nIt is the same with the Magram. They store extra meat so they may fight longer between hunts. If you raid their village to the east and take their stores of meat, then their strength will fail.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSilver Star 200 Feathered Arrow 200 Exploding Shot\nExperience: 1,350","back":"Return after you further prove your worth to the Gelkis!","done":"Good. I can hear the loud Magram bellies grumble from their village, far away!\nI will give this meat to the Gelkis. And we will fight for many days without rest.\nWhat you did is good for the Gelkis, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":36.2,"y":79.2,"n":"Uthek the Wise","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5930":{"id":5930,"t":"Great Bear Spirit","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out the Great Bear Spirit in northwestern Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the bear. When finished, return to Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven, Moonglade.","desc":"In the northwest part of Moonglade resides the home of a wise and noble being we call the Great Bear Spirit. For all druids, it has served as a tutor and mentor into the first true natural understanding of the bear. All druids at one point seek the spirit's wisdom, and you shall be no exception.\nGo to the Great Bear Spirit now and learn what it will teach. When it is satisfied with you, return to me here in Nighthaven. We will then see if you have truly taken account of the lessons it teaches.","rew":"Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Dendrite makes another invisible gesture in the air above him as you approach. Another aura of power comes over him. and he smiles ever so slightly.\n\"I sense wisdom in you, young one, that was not present when we first met. You gaze upon me with strength and knowing intent, though this intent is yet not focused. You will now learn to focus your strength and adopt the nature of the bear into your work.\"","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"170":{"id":170,"t":"A New Threat","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Balir Frosthammer wants you to kill 6 Rockjaw Troggs and 6 Burly Rockjaw Troggs.\nRockjaw Trogg slain : 0/ 6\nBurly Rockjaw Trogg slain : 0/ 6","desc":"I hope you're here to lend us a hand, ‹class›. After the last trogg attack, we could use all the help we can get.\nI hear the buggers have been popping up all across the lands, and it seems Coldridge Valley is no exception. They've been spotted all over the hills to the southeast and near the frozen lake.\nAnd that's not all, just a few nights ago, they attacked and overran our camp to the west!\nWe're a bit shorthanded here, lad/lass, and we need strong arms to help drive the troggs back.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBear Shawl Rustic Belt Snow Boots\nExperience: 170\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Tenacious little buggers, aren't they?","done":"If the problems we've had here are indicative of what is happening elsewhere in our lands, by Magni's beard, we have some troubles ahead of us! I can only hope that the king and Senate are taking steps to deal with the threat the troggs pose.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.7,"y":71.3,"n":"Balir Frosthammer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"90":{"id":90,"t":"Seasoned Wolf Kabobs","lv":25,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 10 Lean Wolf Flanks and return to Chef Grual in Darkshire.\n10 Lean Wolf Flank","desc":"Seasoned Wolf Kabobs are a house favorite! Sure, I can make you some. But first I'll need the supplies. Bring me 10 Lean Wolf Flanks. Given the many wolves here in the forest, I am sure finding the Flanks will be no problem. Fortunately for you, I just received my recent shipment of Stormwind Seasoning Herbs, so all I need are the flanks to get started.","rew":"You will receive:\n4 Seasoned Wolf Kabob Recipe: Seasoned Wolf Kabob\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Were you able to find 10 Lean Wolf Flanks yet? How about the herbs from Felicia in Stormwind?","done":"Very nice work, ‹name›! Enjoy the delicacy known as Seasoned Wolf Kabob!\nDuskwood Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Chef Grual","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"6570":{"id":6570,"t":"Emberstrife","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh and seek out Emberstrife's Den. Once inside, wear the Amulet of Draconic Subversion and speak with Emberstrife.\nProvided: Amulet of Draconic Subversion","desc":"I have attuned this medallion with the magic necessary to create and maintain an illusion within the bounds of the den of Emberstrife.\nEmberstrife is an ancient drake; an old gatekeeper of Nefarian, burdened with the duty to test those dragonspawn that would ascend to the rank of elite guard to Onyxia.\nTravel to the Wyrmbog of Dustwallow Marsh and enter the lair of Emberstrife. Once there, put on the amulet and follow where your destiny may lead!","rew":"Experience: 4,950","done":"Have we run so low on able soldiers that Nefarian is sending me whelps? You will never pass my tests, broodling.\nWestern Plaguelands Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":50.8,"y":77.8,"n":"Myranda the Hag","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":56.7,"y":87.7,"n":"Emberstrife","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"8970":{"id":8970,"t":"I See Alcaz Island In Your Future...","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 20 Bloodkelp from the Strashaz naga and then return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\n20 Bloodkelp Basket of Bloodkelp , Strashaz Serpent Guard 20 % , Strashaz Sorceress 20 % , Strashaz Warrior 20 % and 1 more\nProvided: Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"As I was saying, ‹class›, in my living years I flirted with becoming a diviner. But, there really wasn't as much profit in it as you might imagine, mostly because it's dangerous and the reagents are rare and expensive. However, I do know enough to be able to pinpoint the final piece of the amulet, and the spirit of my former comrade along with it.\nThis is where you come in, ‹name›. I need you to go to Alcaz Island off the coast of Dustwallow Marsh and collect Bloodkelp from the Strashaz naga that live there.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Bloodkelp, ‹name›, a big stack of it, that's what I need to power my divinatory spells. You're likely to need to take at least a couple of friends along with you to Alcaz Island to gather it up... those Strashaz are a nasty lot!","done":"To be honest, ‹name›, I'm surprised you made it back in one piece. Then again, I guess Alcaz Island is the least of your worries right now.\nOk, give me a moment here... divination isn't something that you can just snap your fingers and expect accurate answers from.\nBurning Steppes Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5210":{"id":5210,"t":"Brother Carlin","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Extended Annals of Darrowshire to Carlin Redpath in Eastern Plaguelands.\nExtended Annals of Darrowshire\nProvided: Extended Annals of Darrowshire","desc":"The Annals of Darrowshire, through my magic, has gained pages at its end, and now it extends its history beyond the battle. One of the extra passages tells of another Redpath, Carlin, who survived Joseph's betrayal. Carlin's now in the Plaguelands to the east, at the Light's Hope Chapel.\nTake the book and speak with him.","rew":"Experience: 2,900\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You've come from the west? How fare the rest of Lordaeron? I know that Andorhal is lost, but has the Scourge yet reached fair Tirisfal?","done":"What is this book? The Annals of Darrowshire? That was my home before the war... my home before the battle that destroyed it! Why did you bring me this book?\nBut look here! At the end there are pages that tell tales of the days beyond the battle! Here is a passage about me! And one about my brother Joseph! Is this book true?\nWe must discover the truth!\nWestern Plaguelands Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.5,"y":66.8,"n":"Chromie","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":50,"n":"Carlin Redpath","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"99130":{"id":99130,"t":"An enticing offer","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect ingredients for murloc bait.\n18 Duskweed Petal\n6 Vial of Animal Blood","desc":"I've got a few ideas on how to deal with murlocs. And one of those also helps some others in the process.\nThere's a weed often found on farms in the area called duskweed, and in large quantities the petals are toxic to most animals. If we make some murloc bait with the plant, hopefully that can train those creatures to stay away.\nAnd some farmers get their fields cleared in the process. Truly a win-win... truly a win-win.","rew":"You will receive:\nFightin' Fish\nExperience: 625","back":"Find everything?","done":"Give me just a minute...\nIt's pretty simple bait, but as long as nobody's pet gets into it, it should be safe. Just tell Jason not to eat any of it.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Remy \"Two Times\"","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3130":{"id":3130,"t":"Against the Hatecrest","lv":43,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Latronicus Moonspear in Feathermoon Stronghold.","desc":"At this point, I am going to direct you to my second, Latronicus. He's been keeping a close eye on the naga forces to date. I'll assess the general situation here in regards to the naga; as much as I want to commit a full force to move against them, leaving the stronghold open to direct attack from the Horde - or worse - seems less than optimal.\nAnyway, Latronicus awaits. Good work thus far, ‹name›. Keep it up.\nYou're dismissed.","rew":"Experience: 360\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Excellent, ‹name› - I value a \"can do\" attitude in those who I work with.\nI've been tasked by General Feathermoon to address the naga in a direct manner. My plans are two fold: one, we will weaken their forces both in number and in command, and two, we will uncover what they are up to in the ruins. With your help, we'll counter the naga presence without sacrificing the general security of the stronghold.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Shandris Feathermoon","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":30.4,"y":46.2,"n":"Latronicus Moonspear","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2970":{"id":2970,"t":"Doling Justice","lv":47,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Grimtotem Naturalists, 10 Grimtotem Raiders, and 6 Grimtotem Shamans before returning to Jer'kai Moonweaver in Feralas.\nGrimtotem Naturalist slain : 0/ 12\nGrimtotem Raider slain : 0/ 10\nGrimtotem Shaman slain : 0/ 6","desc":"As she's already told you, Kindal and I will now take the fight to the Grimtotem. Together, we should still be able to pick off some of the tauren without much threat to ourselves, but we'd love some help if you're willing and able.\nYou've seen the camp below us, but there are more to the east. Using your own tactics, deal as much damage to the tauren as you can. We can all meet back here after they've felt the sting of Kindal's arrows and your own weapons.","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Kindal needs time to prepare, but our kills already number in the dozens. The Grimtotem clan is more than aware of our presence in the area, and they seek us out like vipers.\nThey'll do everything in their power to take our heads from our bodies. You should be alert... they'll be coming for you too now that you've interfered.","done":"Kindal was right about you, ‹name›--you do have a knack for this. You are a more seasoned adventurer than the both of us, and for that we thank you.\nThe Grimtotem clan is much more hostile than most tauren... I wonder if their own kind frowns upon their actions. I wouldn't be surprised. As you are probably aware, many races on Azeroth have ties to less kindly counterparts.\nBut that is a discussion for another day.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":65.9,"y":45.6,"n":"Jer'kai Moonweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"3450":{"id":3450,"t":"An Easy Pickup","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Xiggs Fuselighter in Ironforge.","desc":"I want the rubbings delivered to my tower, but there's no need to have you go all the way there. I'll just have them air-lifted out of Azshara.\nXiggs Fuselighter owes me a favor or two and will be in the area soon--he's signed on to patrol the coast. Speak to him before you leave. He can give you a flare gun to signal him with. When you have the rubbings, just head to wherever he tells you and then give them to him so he can get them to my tower safely. He should be in the hangar in the Military Ward.","done":"What can I do for you, ‹name›? Kinda busy at the moment preparing my ship for a long trip. I just came over to see some of the tank pilots--I need some wendigo manes to line my cockpit and they usually have extra.\nI can give you a minute if you're brief... one of the boys just took off to Steelgrill's Depot to see if the pilots down there have extra manes for me.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.1,"y":21.9,"n":"Tymor","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":36.3,"n":"Xiggs Fuselighter","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"250":{"id":250,"t":"A Dark Threat Looms","lv":18,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Investigate the area near the eastern ramp of the Dam and bring Chief Engineer Hinderweir a clue that might reveal what the Dark Iron Dwarves are up to.","desc":"Thank the stars someone is concerned about the well-being of the Dam. First the destruction of the Thandol Span and then the pillaging of Dun Modr! I have no doubt that the Dam will be the target of the next Dark Iron threat. Most of the security detail here was reassigned to the Alliance Front, including my top inspector.\nThat's why I need you, ‹name›. I spotted some Dark Iron Sappers milling about the eastern ramp of the Dam. Investigate the area and bring back a clue.","rew":"Experience: 675\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","done":"The suspicious looking barrel contains a strange smelling powder.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":46,"y":13.6,"n":"Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":56.1,"y":13.2,"n":"Suspicious Barrel","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8650":{"id":8650,"t":"Snowcrown the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":50.7,"n":"Elder Snowcrown","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8250":{"id":8250,"t":"Magecraft","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Sanath Lim-yo and gain passage to see Archmage Xylem.","desc":"Archmage Xylem has been asking around lately... for someone of your experience.\nIf you wish to seek him out, you can find him in Azshara. His tower is built high atop the cliffs, and the only way up is a teleport spell invoked by his arrogant servant, Sanath Lim-yo.\nSanath makes camp below his master's tower. To find him, travel to where Azshara's main road forks at the entrance to the Ruins of Eldarath. From that spot, head directly north until you reach the cliffs.","rew":"You will learn: Teleport to Azshara Tower\nExperience: 500","done":"<Sanath sneers at you.>\nArchmage Xylem awaits your arrival.\nThunder Bluff Undercity Dun Morogh Stormwind City Orgrimmar Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":25.2,"y":21,"n":"Thurston Xane","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":85.4,"y":13.5,"n":"Pierce Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.3,"y":22.2,"n":"Juli Stormkettle","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.2,"y":87.2,"n":"Elsharin","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.8,"y":85.7,"n":"Enyo","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":28.1,"y":50.1,"n":"Sanath Lim-yo","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9050":{"id":9050,"t":"Redemption Wristguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Redemption Wristguards if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Wristguards, 6 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 2 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Wristguards Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Grand Widow Faerlina 0 % in Naxxramas , Anub'Rekhan 0 % in Naxxramas\n6 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n2 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"You will find the remnants of our fallen heroes on the corpses of the Lords of Naxxramas. Bring those desecrated keepsakes to me along with wartorn plate scraps and crafting materials capable of revitalizing the cursed armor and I shall craft a fine piece of armor for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nRedemption Wristguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Redemption Wristguards.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"650":{"id":650,"t":"Ripple Recovery","lv":48,"min":42,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Gilveradin Sunchaser; his camp is located in the Hinterlands.","desc":"The elf you will need to talk to is Gilveradin Sunchaser. He can name any wine, vintage and all, just by smell alone! He can package up the ripple we need, so you'll need to talk with him. We need six bottles for packaging, two for dad, and how ever many he'll want... and believe me, he'll want some. When you've packaged the ripple and got dad's two bottles, come back here!\nGilveradin's camp is near some high elf lodge in the Hinterlands, and those high elves are not good. Trust me.","rew":"Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Ah, so you know Malton? He is an old drinking companion of mine. You see, I have found something that transcends the boundaries of artificial treaties and alliances - alcohol. Were we all to slake our thirsts on its blissful qualities, we all would be in a much better place spiritually.\nAlas, something tells me that your visit here is not to learn of alcohol's redeeming values, now is it.\nOrgrimmar The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":59.8,"y":36.9,"n":"Malton Droffers","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":26.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Gilveradin Sunchaser","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1050":{"id":1050,"t":"Mythology of the Titans","lv":38,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Mythology of the Titans from the Monastery and bring it to Librarian Mae Paledust in Ironforge.\nMythology of the Titans Mythology of the Titans in Scarlet Monastery","desc":"The future is inevitable! We hurl ourselves towards it like falling raindrops to the Great Sea.\nBut perhaps, by studying the past, we can know what to expect and be better prepared for the unknown.\nBefore dire troubles fell upon Lordaeron, there was a bastion of knowledge tucked away in the Tirisfal Glades. It is rumored that a book called Mythology of the Titans was housed in the library of the old Monastery.\nBring it to me and perhaps together we can unlock the secrets of the past!","rew":"You will receive:\nExplorers' League Commendation\nExperience: 3,550\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"The Monastery was a seminary for Paladins-in-training. Once a stronghold of the Light, it fell into the hands of the crazed zealots of the Scarlet Crusade.\nThe Crusade believed their goal a noble one: to purify the land of the undead plague. But insanity tainted their plight and now they stand enemies to all.\nBring Mythology of the Titans to me so I can study it and house it here in Ironforge.\nThe corrupt halls of the Monastery are no place for such a historical treasure.","done":"You have rescued the sacred text!\nYour journey was long and acquiring the book was undoubtedly no easy task. But the dwarves of Ironforge stand to benefit from your success.\nThank you, ‹name›, on behalf of the Explorers' League.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.1,"y":23.1,"n":"Librarian Mae Paledust","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scarlet-monastery"]},"1530":{"id":1530,"t":"Call of Water","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Brine in Southern Barrens.","desc":"If there is one lesson you must learn of water, it is this: water means rebirth.\nIts power flows, erodes, and makes clean all manner of things. You will find its ability to heal and replenish incomparable, but only when it is pure.\nWhen you understand that water, when polluted, can devastate all that it touches, you will appreciate how vital a resource it is.\nIf you wish the water sapta, find Brine deep in Southern Barrens. Her home is continually molested by the quilboar there.","rew":"Experience: 440","done":"Yes?\nMmm. I have a feeling I know what you're going to ask me: what would possess someone to live out here in the deepest part of the Barrens, the threat of quilboar all around, and no protection? Well, we all have our reasons to justify why we act the way we do. The real question is, what brings a lowly ‹race› to the deepest reaches of the Barrens to speak to a woman who obviously has no concern for her own well-being?\nI'm willing to bet we both know the answer to that.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":43.4,"y":77.4,"n":"Brine","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8410":{"id":8410,"t":"Elemental Mastery","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 52 instead of 50.","obj":"Collect a sample of air, fire, earth and water for Bath'rah the Windwatcher.\nElemental Air Whirlwind Shredder 84.8 % , Whirlwind Stormwalker 83.7 % , Swirling Vortex 80 % , Whirlwind Ripper 79 % and 4 more\nElemental Fire Baron Charr 69.9 % , Prince Skaldrenox 42.7 % , Baron Geddon 30 % , Sulfuron Harbinger 30 % and 4 more\nElemental Earth Avalanchion 77.1 % , Baron Kazum 50.9 % , Rumbling Exile 11.1 % , Rock Elemental 11.1 % and 4 more\nElemental Water Princess Tempestria 73.9 % , Lord Skwol 46.7 % , Seeker Aqualon 26.9 % , Hydrospawn 26 % and 4 more","desc":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher has sent out a summons for a shaman of your wisdom. He requests you bring a sample of each of the elements to show you are ready.\nTo find Bath'rah, go to the river east of Tarren Mill. Follow the river north until you come across the ruins where Bath'rah resides.","rew":"Experience: 3,800","back":"What you got for me, ‹class›?","done":"Excellent, mon. Now we be talkin'.\nSwamp of Sorrows Thunder Bluff Orgrimmar Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":48.2,"y":57.9,"n":"Haromm","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":22.8,"y":21.1,"n":"Siln Skychaser","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":23.6,"y":18.8,"n":"Tigor Skychaser","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":22,"y":18.8,"n":"Beram Skychaser","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.8,"y":36.4,"n":"Kardris Dreamseeker","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":37.8,"y":36.5,"n":"Sian'tsu","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.7,"y":35.9,"n":"Sagorne Creststrider","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.5,"y":66.9,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8810":{"id":8810,"t":"Bandages for the Field","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 30 Heavy Runecloth Bandages, 30 Heavy Silk Bandages and 30 Heavy Mageweave Bandages to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing X in order to complete this quest.\n30 Heavy Runecloth Bandage sold by Jimmy McWeaksauce\n30 Heavy Mageweave Bandage\n30 Heavy Silk Bandage\nLogistics Task Briefing X\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing X","desc":"Our supply of bandages in the battlefield is running dangerously low after the recent casualties we have incurred. Obtain a batch of first-aid supplies and deliver them to Windcaller Proudhorn in Cenarion Hold.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something for me, ‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"330":{"id":330,"t":"Patrol Schedules","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Corporal Sethman.","desc":"The note you gave me is signed with an \"-M\"...I don't know what that could mean.\nBut...the note also says this person shared patrol routes with Thorsen last week. So whoever shared patrol with Thorsen last week must be the traitor!\nGo to Corporal Sethman. He handles the patrol schedules and can tell you who was with Thorsen.","rew":"Experience: 290","done":"Oh, yes I can check that for you. Let's see...last week it was...\n...why, it was Private Merle scheduled with Thorsen. They had the same patrol times all of last week.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3,"n":"Lieutenant Doren","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":37.7,"y":3.4,"n":"Corporal Sethman","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"570":{"id":570,"t":"Mok'thardin's Enchantment","lv":38,"min":33,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Far Seer Mok'thardin at the Grom'gol base camp wants 8 Shadowmaw Claws and a Pristine Tigress Fang.\n8 Shadowmaw Claw Shadowmaw Panther 80 % , Elder Shadowmaw Panther 80 %\nPristine Tigress Fang Stranglethorn Tigress 15 %","desc":"The power of the jungle's magic must be realized and then harnessed by the Horde. My rituals have proven successful so far. I can cast very powerful enchantments. For you, brave ‹class›, I shall make a special item indeed.\nBring to me some Shadowmaw Panther claws along with a Tigress fang. Not just any fang will do. It must be in pristine condition.\nThe beasts lurk throughout the jungle but you will find some close by, just across the river from Mizjah Ruins to the southeast.","rew":"Experience: 2,150\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"What news do you bring?","done":"Your knowledge of the jungle is strong, ‹name›. These specimens will be perfect. I will thank the spirits for sacrificing such fine beasts for the cause of the Horde.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.1,"y":29.2,"n":"Far Seer Mok'thardin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"95770":{"id":95770,"t":"Locating the lost city","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Explore the Vile Reef and find the cavern entrance.","desc":"After rereading the legend, it doesn't seem like we are in the wrong place for the lost city, but perhaps there is yet some detail that has been overlooked.\nIn my younger years I used to dive in the Vile Reef ruins, but that was before the murlocs settled there. If memory serves there was a cavern there.\nI have heard that there are now naga gathering in that region, which is unusual. I want to know what has lured them there.\nGo and explore just west of the Vile Reef and return to me with any news.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar\nLevel 40 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 36 38 43 51 Side Horde Shareable Yes Quest ID 95770","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1690":{"id":1690,"t":"Wastewander Justice","lv":43,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take down 10 Wastewander Bandits and Thieves east of Gadgetzan, then report back to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle.\nWastewander Bandit slain : 0/ 10\nWastewander Thief slain : 0/ 10","desc":"You there! It's time for you to be a big helper to the Gadgetzan Water Company.\nThe Wastewander nomads out in the Tanaris desert have seized almost all the water wells! Without access to them, our water supply will dry up in no time. If you want to get in our good graces, then you'll help us bring justice to those nomads!\nHead east of here and bring down ten Wastewander Bandits and Thieves, then report back to me on the double. Justice waits for no man... goblin... bah, just get on it!","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Back so soon? I hope you were able to bring some goblin-style justice to those Wastewander Bandits and Thieves like I asked you to!","done":"Now that's what I call efficiency! You've helped thin out the nomad's numbers enough now that we can start to think about how we can win back those water wells.\nThe Gadgetzan Water Company thanks you for your help, but we're far from done in dealing with those foul nomads. Listen close - here's what we need next...","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":28.5,"n":"Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"10":{"id":10,"t":"The Scrimshank Redemption","lv":48,"min":39,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Discover the fate of Junior Surveyor Scrimshank, and bring either him or his surveying equipment to Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser in Gadgetzan.\nScrimshank's Surveying Gear Scrimshank's Surveying Gear","desc":"Oh, this is just terrible! I sent out my top assistant, Junior Surveyor Scrimshank, into the desert southeast of here. That's an area we call the Gaping Chasm. Well, he's gone missing, and his last report had more of those weird bugs where he was. Could it be that they've infested two major regions of the desert now?\nI need you to head into the Gaping Chasm and look for Scrimshank, please! That... or at least find his surveying equipment. I fear that may be all that is left of the poor sod.","rew":"Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Well, what news do you have? You look like you've been in quite the fight... is Scrimshank alive?","done":"He was a good goblin, young Scrimshank. Let's hope that his demise was not in vain by what he was able to record with his surveying equipment.\nIt seems as though we have quite the situation on our hands here with these bugs. They're way too cunning for their own good, and the research we've done so far is shaping up to indicate that they might even be under the controlling influence of a third party! If this is the case, then it bodes ill for not only Gadgetzan, but the whole desert!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.2,"y":27.5,"n":"Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"490":{"id":490,"t":"Bounty gnarlpine furbolg","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Shayla Nightbreeze on the road outside of Darnassus wants you to bring her 20 Gnarlpine Fangs.\n20 Gnarlpine Fang","desc":"By strict orders from the Sentinels, I am commissioning a bounty on the Gnarlpine. They are no longer friends of the forest. Their corruption has left them mindless threats to our people and the creatures of the glade.\nAs decreed, you shall be rewarded for removing the furbolg menaces from Teldrassil. Bring to me their fangs as proof of your deeds.\nYou will find furbolg concentrated in Ban'ethil Hollow, west of Dolanaar and south of the road, and in Starbreeze Village to the east.","rew":"Money: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Teldrassil cannot thrive with corruption tainting the land. Drive the Gnarlpine from this forest, once and for all.","done":"You have served well, Fuzzy. You shall be rewarded for your contribution.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":38.4,"y":54,"n":"Sentinel Shayla Nightbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"99050":{"id":99050,"t":"The great tree provides","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 Dewy Lasher Fronds, an Empty Vial, and a Refreshing Spring Water for Byancie in Dolanaar.\n6 Dewy Lasher Frond\nEmpty Vial\nRefreshing Spring Water","desc":"I will need your help acquiring the ingredients I need to stop the affliction long enough for Eralya to make it back here for further treatment.\nThankfully, our living home is still bountiful and will provide in our time of need.\nThe core ingredient is dewy lasher fronds. You'll find them around Lake Al'Ameth directly south of here, or Wellspring Lake and its river to the northwest.\nIn addition, I'll need an empty vial and some spring water. Both can be bought here in town, or traded for.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 0 silver, 85 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Do you have the ingredients? I fear Eralya may not have long.","done":"Thank you for your help. Please, accept this to help with the costs of the vial and water.\nNow, to make the salve. It should only take a moment.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Byancie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"890":{"id":890,"t":"The Missing Shipment","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Gazlowe's Ledger to Wharfmaster Dizzywig.\nGazlowe's Ledger\nProvided: Gazlowe's Ledger","desc":"I've been waiting forever for my last shipment of goods from Booty Bay! I'm pretty sure that it must have been stolen by the Freebooters, but just to make sure, will you go down to the dockside and ask Dizzywig if my goods were already put into my warehouse without my knowledge?\nHere, take my ledger down to Dizzywig and have him double check my inventory records against his logs.","rew":"Experience: 100\n+10 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Wares to send on the next ship, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, Gazlowe sent you, did he? Just a moment, let me take a look here and check my own logs and make sure I didn't have Gazlowe's shipment sent to the wrong place.\nBet he's waiting for those boots from Drizzlek...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.2,"n":"Gazlowe","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.4,"y":38.5,"n":"Wharfmaster Dizzywig","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"3370":{"id":3370,"t":"In Nightmares","lv":25,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 10 instead of 15.","obj":"Bring the Nightmare Shard to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus.\nNightmare Shard\nProvided: Nightmare Shard","desc":"This shard holds great secrets; it is the pure essence of the Emerald Dream. However, what I see in this shard is not a dream; one would call this sort of a vision a nightmare.\nI do not wish to alarm you, ‹name›, but I think it is best if you deliver this shard into the hands of a wise druid as soon as you can...\nMathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Circle is who you need to find. Head to Darnassus. I cannot say more.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTalbar Mantle Quagmire Galoshes\nExperience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"May I help you with something?","done":"Falla sent you to me? Well now, let's see that shard that you say she was so hesitant to talk about...\n<Mathrengyl peers into the shard>\nOh... I didn't... Well.\n‹name›, thank you for delivering this to me. It isn't wise to speak of things such as this, though, I advise you. These are matters that the Cenarion druids alone must attend to.\nLet's just say that things in the Emerald Dream are not as we thought...\nPerhaps in the future, our paths may cross again.\nThe Barrens Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":48.2,"y":32.8,"n":"Falla Sagewind","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1450":{"id":1450,"t":"Gryphon Master Talonaxe","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Gryphon Master Talonaxe inside the Aerie Peak Aviary.","desc":"So you're a glorified errand boy/girl for some old Explorers' League geezer, eh?\nWell you listen to me, ‹class›. I don't know who your old buddy was flying around with down in Azeroth. Do I look like Gryphon Master Talonaxe to you? Do I?\nIf you're so interested in the flight assignments why don't you ask the gryphon master? If I catch you idling around here for much longer, I'm going to put you to some real work.\nNow get a move on.","rew":"Experience: 900","done":"Ah, yes. Of course I remember sending one of my gryphon riders to lend a hand to Brohann Caskbelly.\nAlways had a soft spot in my heart for the Explorers' League. My father helped with the initial excavation team that discovered Uldaman as a matter of fact.\nI sent who I thought was my best gryphon rider at the time with Brohann. He was a chap by the name of Rhapsody Shindigger.\nAnd what a gryphon jockey he was! Well until...","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":11.8,"y":46.8,"n":"Falstad Wildhammer","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":9.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Gryphon Master Talonaxe","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"7850":{"id":7850,"t":"Dark Vessels","lv":50,"min":46,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Primal Torntusk at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to recover 10 Vessels of Tainted Blood from Jintha'alor. Return to Primal Torntusk when this task is complete.\n10 Vessel of Tainted Blood Vessel of Tainted Blood","desc":"The Vilebranch fight with supernatural ferocity. This is due to the foul magical weavings of the Vile Priestess Hexx.\nThroughout Jintha'alor you will find dark vessels of tainted blood. The vessels radiate the foul magic of the faceless blood God, empowering the Vilebranch and also driving them to madness.\nSteal those vessels and return them to me so that I may remove the taint and ultimately loosen the grip of the blood God.","rew":"You will receive:\nNature's Breath\nExperience: 5,900\n+150 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"Be cautious in battling the Vilebranch, ‹name›. Their minds are clouded - they fight to the death.","done":"The dark energy that compels the Vilebranch has been lifted - for now. We must remain ever vigilant in our battle against evil, as even if the Vile Priestess is destroyed, another soon takes her place.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":78.2,"y":81.2,"n":"Primal Torntusk","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1130":{"id":1130,"t":"Melor Sends Word","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"‹name›, Melor Stonehoof has heard of your deeds, and has set a path before you.\nIf you wish to take it, then go to Thunder Bluff and speak with Melor. You will find him on Hunter's Rise.","done":"So, ‹name›, you have come. Now, are you prepared to journey through distant lands?\nIf so, young ‹class›, then listen on...\nThe Barrens Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":61.5,"y":80.9,"n":"Melor Stonehoof","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"410":{"id":410,"t":"The Dormant Shade","lv":10,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Candle of Beckoning Silverback Patriarch","back":"This is an old, beaten, bloody table.","done":"You place the Candle of Beckoning upon the table and light it...","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":66.6,"y":44.9,"n":"Lillith's Dinner Table","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"97290":{"id":97290,"t":"Unending torment","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report your findings to Master Apothecary Faranell in Undercity.","desc":"You... abomination...\nWhy should... help you...\nBe gone...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSlain Baron's Signet Grave Shroud Monstrous Cleaver\nMoney: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,650","done":"Not cooperating, eh? Excellent. I always love a challenge.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":46,"y":62.2,"n":"Unfinished Abomination","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":48.4,"y":69.4,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"65610":{"id":65610,"t":"Wish you were here","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Investigate Fallen Sky Lake in Ashenvale and report your findings to Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.\nWithered Scarf","desc":"I met Krilge while making Mooncloth in Ashenvale. He was stationed there to protect civilians from danger, until he disappeared...\nThey've stopped looking for him and consider him a deserter, but I don't believe it.\nWe would often meet at Fallen Sky Lake before it became overrun by those aggressive bog beasts.\nI'm not typically one to ask favors, but if you could go to Ashenvale and look for any sign of him, I'd appreciate it.","back":"Yes, what is it?","done":"What is it you have there, ‹name›? A scarf made of... Mooncloth? You best not be seeking to romance me.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":63.4,"y":50,"n":"Magar","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":45.6,"n":"Gan'rul Bloodeye","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4490":{"id":4490,"t":"Summon Felsteed","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 320 experience instead of 300, 1.07 times as much.","obj":"Speak to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet to learn the ability to summon a Felsteed.","desc":"I would give you a reward for your patience and hard work. But know this, the ability to summon a Felsteed will be much more difficult in the future. You will have to earn it... and it will not be easy.\nFor now, go with the power to summon such a creature and use it as you see fit.","rew":"You will learn: Summon Felsteed\nExperience: 320","done":"Good luck, ‹name›. I look forward to seeing you in the future.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"8570":{"id":8570,"t":"Past Efforts in Warsong Gulch","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Warsong Gulch Ribbon of Sacrifice","desc":"Ah, yes! Of course we wouldn't forget about your past accomplishments in Warsong Gulch.","rew":"You will receive:\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor\nLevel 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Horde Shareable Yes Quest ID 8570","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5050":{"id":5050,"t":"Good Luck Charm","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Janice Felstone in Western Plaguelands her Good Luck Half-Charm.\nGood Luck Half-Charm\nProvided: Good Luck Half-Charm","desc":"It would seem that I was wrong about you ‹name›, and for that I owe you an apology. My sister sent me a number of personal effects, including humorously enough the deed to the Felstone farm. I think I'll pass on reclaiming it right now.\nIf my sister's spirit remains tethered to the farm and cannot rest, please... could you return this to her? It is half of a good luck charm she had, with her husband having the other half.\nMaybe her knowing I have these things will now put her soul to rest.","rew":"Experience: 2,550","back":"John, sweetheart... is that you? I'm so cold all the sudden...","done":"You give the half-charm back to the apparition. She looks at it, then at you expectantly.\n\"Honey, where did you put your half of the charm? We can't be together unless we have both halves. Honey... can you see me?\"\nStormwind City Undercity Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":60.2,"y":57,"n":"Ol' Emma","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":67.6,"y":44.2,"n":"Jeremiah Payson","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":38.4,"y":54.1,"n":"Janice Felstone","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"4810":{"id":4810,"t":"Return to Tinkee","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Felnok's Package to Tinkee Steamboil in the Burning Steppes.\nFelnok's Package\nProvided: Felnok's Package","desc":"Ok, everything is prepared and packed and ready for transport! Good luck in your journey, and make sure you tell Tinkee that she owes me!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlitzcleaver Grave Scepter\nExperience: 2,700\n+50 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"‹name›! Did you talk to Felnok? Did you bring the components I need?","done":"You brought them! Great! I'll get to work right away! Thanks a ton, ‹name›!\nYou've been so helpful to me, I might need you for even more important tasks later...\nWinterspring Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.6,"y":38.6,"n":"Felnok Steelspring","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.2,"y":24,"n":"Tinkee Steamboil","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"4970":{"id":4970,"t":"Frostsaber Provisions","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 5 Shardtooth Meats and 5 Chillwind Meats for Rivern Frostwind in Winterspring.\n5 Shardtooth Meat Rabid Shardtooth 62 % , Elder Shardtooth 52 % , Shardtooth Bear 42 % , Shardtooth Mauler 32 %\n5 Chillwind Meat Fledgling Chillwind 50 % , Chillwind Chimaera 50 % , Chillwind Ravager 50 %","desc":"If you wish to prove yourself, you may begin by doing a very simple, but very important task.\nGather meat from the chimaera and from the shardtooth bears in the area. Bring it to me so that I may use it to feed the frostsabers that are being trained.","back":"Discipline and determination are your goals. I may ask you to do a simple task many times; you must perform to the best of your ability each time.","done":"Thank you for assisting me, ‹name›. My opinion of you grows as time passes.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":49.9,"y":9.8,"n":"Rivern Frostwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"94490":{"id":94490,"t":"Ripped missive","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Ripped Missive to Elegael Thornpaw in the Shadowgale Forest.\nRipped Missive","desc":"<Tucked behind one of Haalien's bracers is a note that's been slightly torn and bloodstained in your fight. It looks like it contains useful information for about the cultist motivations for the attack on the druid den. Elegael would be interested in this intel.>","done":"They were here for the pylon? But to what end? We were not the original reason for their attack?\n<Elegael trails off shaking with rage as she reads.>\nThey murdered my people because we were an inconvenience! I shall tear apart every cultist with my fangs! I will make sure none leave this place with their lives.\nGo, swiftly! If the orders truly originated in Valanaar, it means it is likely a traitor hiding there. Give the missive to Lotheluum in Valannar and tell him what has transpired.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.6,"y":39.2,"n":"Elegael Thornpaw","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"9210":{"id":9210,"t":"The Savage Guard - Arcanum of Focus","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Zanza the Restless in Zul'Gurub wants an Arcanum of Focus.\nArcanum of Focus","desc":"Zanza can create many ancient troll enchantments with proper components! Have you heard of the Savage Guard? No, of course you haven't. Your mind is addled with the inferior elven magic.\nBring me an arcanum of elven creation so that I may destroy the aberration. Do this and the Savage Guard will be yours.","rew":"You will receive:\nSavage Guard\n+200 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Do you have the arcanum?","done":"The worthless magic in these enchantments fuels my anger. My anger gives me strength.\nBring me more and you shall receive another Savage Guard.\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 9210","cats":["zulgurub"]}});